## Summary

**Task:** Pass the MXFS ship gate. On entry: 11/12 PASS, only `rsync_paired` failing (4-node parallel rsync must run within 1.2× single-node XFS ≈ 5567ms/node; cache_coherency now passes).

**Major proven win this session (KEEP, build `3AE2BA36`+):** Found and fixed the catastrophic serialization. The directory-inode allocator used a **cluster-wide rotor** (`xfs_dialloc_pick_ag`), scattering every node's directories across all 20 AGs → multiple nodes' dirs shared AGs → cross-node AGI/AGF CAW ping-pong. Regular files were already node-affine (sess45); directories weren't. Confirmed the scatter directly via `tools/chk_mxfs -v` (allocations spread into AGs 4,5,10,17,19 with only 4 nodes). **Fix:** in multi-node, dirs also pin to `node_slot % maxagi`. **Result: 540s+ (never completed) → ~30s, all 8714 files, EC=0, zero corruption — ~18× faster.**

**Still failing on ratio (~658%).** Decisive RULE-4 measurements isolated the residual as **per-op multi-node DLM/FUA cost, not contention**: solo rsync with peers idle = 22s vs 4.8s single-node-alone (so ~17s is per-op overhead). A new diagnostic param `inode_caw_local=1` showed **per-file-inode CAW grants cost ~7.7s** (8714 new files each do disk find_slot/read_slot/caw_slot); the remaining ~9.4s is FUA metadata reads (correctness-load-bearing — `fua_disable` hangs) + AG/dir locks + durability.

**Next (queued at relay boundary):** The workload is fully node-private, so it *should* run like single-node. The architectural fix is to make metadata ops on objects in an AG a node owns EX local (no per-op CAW/FUA) — GFS2 resource-group model; node-affine AGs are the foundation. The safety crux (inode vs AG locks are independent CAW resources; cache_coherency must not regress) makes this a RULE-5 consult — I was loading `ask_gemini` to get the safe protocol. Likely-safe subset: regular-file inode grants local-when-AG-owned, keep directory grants real, flush+release on AG BAST.

**Also this session:** recorded the user correction (use MXFS's own tools, never `xfs_db`/`xfs_info`) in CLAUDE.md + a new memory; gated the always-on per-dir-op `P-DIR-SEQ FASTEX` printk behind `mxfs.instr`.

